WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.129 --> 00:00:09.600
Speaker 1: You all know that I am in general&nbsp;
a pragmatist. I am a sort of realpolitik&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:16.480
realist. I understand that change often comes&nbsp;
in small steps. I don't want to let the perfect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:23.600
become the enemy of the good. But it may&nbsp;
be time for progressives to kill what is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:30.720
increasingly a gutted infrastructure and spending&nbsp;
bill because there is almost nothing left in it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:40.000
Paid leave has now fallen out of the democratic&nbsp;
package in an urgent scramble, as described by CNN&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.560
to secure centrist Democratic Senator Joe Manchin&nbsp;
support. Democrats are expected to scrap paid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:54.880
family and medical leave from their cornerstone&nbsp;
economic and climate package, discarding one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.880 --> 00:01:00.800
the central planks of Joe Biden's proposal as they&nbsp;
scramble to strike a deal with holdout senators.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.520
The plan's survival has been in question for&nbsp;
several days due to objections from Joe Manchin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:11.440
Biden's initial 12 week proposal of paid leave&nbsp;
was scaled back to four weeks to try to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:18.320
Joe Manchin support that was rejected. Kirsten&nbsp;
Gillibrand tried to find a compromise with margin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:23.520
that didn't work. One of the people said,&nbsp;
prompting Democrats to push it out of the package&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.520
as they seek to scale back the proposals overall&nbsp;
cost and programs to meet mansion's demand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.080
Manchin made clear he would not move when&nbsp;
asked about the provision, saying I just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:41.040
can't do it. And now, as we're filming, this&nbsp;
is about to happen. Joe Biden is expected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:47.440
to announce new social spending and new social&nbsp;
spending framework to try to get every Democrat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:56.400
on board. The steps that we are now talking about,&nbsp;
the increments that we are now talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:05.280
are so small in terms of what's left of this&nbsp;
bill that we may mostly have a pseudo slush fund&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:11.840
for some projects called infrastructure. It'll&nbsp;
be counted as a political win for the centrist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:18.960
Democrats. It'll be counted as a political win for&nbsp;
Republicans by having been able to get all sorts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:25.040
of stuff removed. And it's going to be barely&nbsp;
anything, and I am essentially ready to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:30.720
you know, it has some things in it that&nbsp;
makes sense. But the big picture is now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:36.720
so dire. It's so grim. It's so pathetic that&nbsp;
it may be time to kill this bill and say, Hey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.400
you need us progressives for this too, and&nbsp;
you're losing us. What has been removed so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:48.160
far? My best under you? It's actually hard to&nbsp;
encapsulate everything that's been removed so far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.960
for a bunch of different reasons, including that&nbsp;
there were different bills that contain these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:58.800
things in different negotiations. Paid family&nbsp;
leave seems to be gone or will be gone soon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.440
A tuition free community college. We already&nbsp;
learned days ago last week that's gone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:11.760
A serious climate regulations gone. Expanded&nbsp;
Medicare eligibility gun. The vision hearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.720
dental stuff that Joe Biden talked about doesn't&nbsp;
seem to be in their prescription drug price&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:25.120
controls. Nope. Universal child care plus making&nbsp;
permanent the tax credit gone. Some kind of tax&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.680
to target the very, very, very richest Americans&nbsp;
now that are not going to be part of this bill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:38.720
apparently, either. So listen, I get it. This is&nbsp;
very rare that I say actually overall because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:44.240
a message that needs to be sent. Nothing kind of&nbsp;
makes more sense than the scraps that are left.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:48.480
Rarely am I at that point. People who have been&nbsp;
following the show for a long time know that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:56.640
but it might be time with this bill because this&nbsp;
is going to. It'll count as something was done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:04.160
when it's two percent, five percent, not by&nbsp;
dollar value, but in terms of the components.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.960
Five percent of what it was supposed to be&nbsp;
done. And everybody but the left gets a win.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:13.200
Republicans who want nothing done well, they&nbsp;
almost get a win if this passes because there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.080
almost nothing left of it. Centrists get what&nbsp;
they want because they've managed to get all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.640
of the important stuff or most of the important&nbsp;
stuff out of it or scale it down or whatever. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:28.400
I am understanding, you know, I know other shows&nbsp;
pretend that the country is way more left than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:32.560
it actually is. And all this different stuff. I&nbsp;
don't do that here. I feel like one of the things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:37.680
I try to do is give you an honest and accurate&nbsp;
assessment of where is the country on a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:44.000
these issues. The country is well to the left&nbsp;
of this bill. There is no doubt about it. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:50.720
what we have at this point is I don't know if the&nbsp;
term pyrrhic victory even applies because I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:58.080
know that it's a victory, even a pyrrhic one.&nbsp;
I want to hear from you. Is this something that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:04.480
any progressive that has the ability to vote no&nbsp;
should be voting no on because it's become so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:11.040
endlessly pathetic? Let me know your thoughts.&nbsp;
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.560
We're going to take a quick break, and&nbsp;
we have much more coming up for you today

